(vector (map (:db/id -1)
 (:adr/id "adr-2609070200-capability-provider-status-is-a-claim")
 (:adr/title "A capability package's declared provider-status is a claim; only the host tables are evidence")
 (:adr/status "accepted")
 (:adr/date "2026-09-07")
 (:adr/body "## Context\n\n`orgs/kotoba-lang/capability-llm-infer/capability.edn` declared\n`:capability/provider-status :contract-only`, and `kotoba-lang/murakumo`'s\n`murakumo.app.edn` cited that status as the reason every LLM turn of the\nitonami agent stays OFF the mesh, on a JVM resident.\n\nMeasured 2026-09-06, the declaration was half stale and half true, and nothing\nin the tree could separate the halves:\n\n- `kototama/src/kototama/tender.clj` implements `llm-infer-host-fn`, metered.\n- `kototama/src/kototama/browser.cljc` records `:llm-infer {:jvm :yes :browser :yes :node :inject}`.\n- `kotoba-lang/lang/host-parity.edn` records the same import as `:browser :no`.\n- `kotoba/src/kotoba/wasm_exec.clj` had no implementation and\n  `kotoba/src/kotoba/runtime.clj` no `op->kind` entry, so the Chicory host the\n  mesh actually uses could not serve it.\n- `kotoba-lang/src/kotoba/lang/capability_values.cljc` had no llm kind at all,\n  which would have denied the op at RUN time with `:unsupported-kind` even had\n  the other halves existed.\n\nFive sources, four different answers, one declaration, and no way to ask.\n\n## Decision\n\n`scripts/verify-capability-provider-status.cljs` measures, for every\nchecked-out `capability-*` package, whether a host provider actually exists,\nand reports three kinds of disagreement: `understated` (declares\n`:contract-only`, a host table shows a provider), `overstated` (declares a\nprovider status, no host table implements it), and `inconsistent` (two host\ntables disagree about the same host/op pair).\n\nIt reports that sources DISAGREE. It does not rule that a repository is wrong.\n\nRegistered in `manifest/orgs-detectors.edn` as\n`:verify-capability-provider-status`. It cannot be a murakumo fleet gate: it\nreads `orgs/`, and the fleet ships one repository's tree to a node.\n\n## The detector had the defect it was built to find\n\nFirst run, 2026-09-07: `SCANNED 61/61`, `FINDINGS 0`, clean, exit 0.\n\n`load-capability` returns the package under `:data`; the reporting path read\nit as `(:cap %)`. `classify` therefore received `nil` sixty-one times, a nil\npackage has no `:ops`, and no observation was ever made. Zero findings from\nzero work is byte-identical to zero findings from a complete sweep.\n\nCalling `classify` directly on `capability-llm-infer` returned two findings by\nhand -- understated (tender and both browser tables show a provider against a\n`:contract-only` declaration) and inconsistent (`kototama.browser` says\n`:browser :yes`, `host-parity.edn` says `:browser :no`). With the read\ncorrected, the same invocation reports findings and exits 1.\n\nThis is ADR-2608136000's first question, answered wrong by the very check\nwritten to ask it. Recorded here rather than quietly fixed, because the shape\nis what generalises: a classifier that is handed nothing returns the same\nvalue as a classifier that found nothing.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Exit is three-valued: 0 clean, 1 findings, 2 REFUSED. REFUSED covers an\n  unreadable host table, an unreadable `west.yml`, no `capability-*` checkout,\n  and any checked-out package that could not be measured -- every verdict\n  depends on all seven sources, so a partial read is a lower bound.\n- A self-check runs before any scan and exercises five classifier arms against\n  fixtures; if it cannot discriminate, the run REFUSES rather than reporting.\n- `SCANNED` is over checkouts, not over the workspace: `orgs/` is\n  west-managed, an unchecked-out project is invisible to the filesystem, and\n  the detector prints a NOTE saying its absence is not evidence.\n- No finding count is recorded in this ADR or in the registry entry. This\n  workspace has repeatedly had dated measurements quoted later with the date\n  dropped; what is recorded is how to measure.\n\n## Related\n\nThe `llm/infer` half of the original finding was closed the same day: the\nprovider now exists on this workspace's JVM/Chicory host\n(`kotoba-lang/kotoba` merge `868f3fb`, with `:host/llm-infer` registered in\n`kotoba-lang`'s `effect-for-kind`), so `capability-llm-infer`'s own\n`:capability/provider-status` is now the stale side of a disagreement this\ndetector reports.")))
